---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import AhlemAvatar from "../assets/ahlem2.jpeg";
import { SectionTitle } from "./UI";
---

<section id="about" class="w-full min-h-screen px-6 py-4 pt-14 bg-background">
    <SectionTitle
        title="About Me"
        color="primary"
        className="h-screen flex flex-col justify-center"
    >
        <div class="flex_center flex-col lg:flex-row w-full h-full py-10 gap-8">
           <Image
    src={AhlemAvatar}  
    alt="About_Avatar"
    class="Fade_Up rounded-full scale-x-[-1] lg:mx-14"
    width={225}
    height={225}
    loading="lazy"
/>


            <div
                class="Fade_Up w-full md:w-[80%] lg:w-[60%] flex justify-center items-start flex-col gap-4 lg:border-l border-primary py-8 lg:pl-10"
            >
                <h2 class="Fade_Up text-[1.5em] font-bold">Building practical AI products with full-stack foundations.</h2>
                <p class="Fade_Up text-justify">
                    I am Ahlem Bouchahoua, a computer engineering student specialized in AI and software development. My work focuses on turning intelligent systems into usable, secure, and production-ready web platforms.
                </p>
                <p class="Fade_Up text-justify">
                    My recent PFE project is an AI-assisted IT audit platform developed in a PwC Tunisia context, combining React, TypeScript, FastAPI, LangChain, Azure OpenAI, Azure AI Search, Azure SQL, Blob Storage, Docker, and Microsoft Entra ID.
                </p>
                <p class="Fade_Up text-justify">
                    I enjoy building end-to-end products: clean interfaces, reliable APIs, AI workflows, cloud-ready architecture, and features that solve real business problems instead of staying at prototype level.
                </p>
                <p class="Fade_Up text-justify">
                    I am currently looking for opportunities where I can contribute as a junior software engineer, full-stack developer, or AI application developer.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

